titl borrows ideas, and in places adapts small pieces of logic, from these projects. Their licences require
that the copyright notice and licence text stay with copies or substantial portions of their code.

- stable-ts (https://github.com/jianfch/stable-ts), MIT License. Relative word-duration clamping
  (WhisperResult.clamp_max) and the ignore_special_periods idea. Used in titl/timing.py and titl/segment.py.
- srt_equalizer (https://github.com/peterk/srt_equalizer), MIT License. Reference for splitting long
  subtitles to a target length.
- WhisperX (https://github.com/m-bain/whisperX), BSD-2-Clause. Reference for per-language conjunction
  and comma handling when splitting subtitles.

Their full licence texts are in their repositories and in the source distributions on PyPI.
